:name: nucleus-embedded-nrf
:description: Inject input.bin, load a GENERATED embedded-pattern nRF52840 firmware, run bounded, capture UARTE0.

# The Renode runtime script for the embedded-pattern backend's SECOND-MCU-
# family (nRF52840) bin (P10, TASK-0453.10). The sibling of
# tests/renode/embedded/run.resc (STM32H7): same example-agnostic shape, but
# a Nordic nRF52840 (Cortex-M4F) co-simulated machine whose UARTE0 EasyDMA
# transmit Renode captures to a file backend. The ELF this loads is GENERATED
# by `nucleus build --backend embedded-pattern --shim nrf52840` from a PRD
# §11 single-worker example (01-elementwise-add naive); this script injects
# whatever $input fixture it is handed into the RAM window @ 0x2002_0000,
# loads whatever $bin ELF it is handed, and captures UARTE0 verbatim — the
# firmware loads its REAL input from the injected region, computes the
# example's kernels, and EasyDMA-streams the RAW output bytes over UARTE0;
# the `renode-embedded-nrf` just recipe `cmp`s the captured bytes BYTE-EXACT
# against the example's reference.bin (PRD §10.3 point 3).
#
# Caller injects three path variables before `include`-ing this script:
#   $bin      = @<path to the cross-compiled GENERATED firmware ELF>
#   $uartFile = @<path the UARTE0 file backend writes to>
#   $input    = @<path to the chosen example's input.bin fixture>

mach create "nrf"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/nrf52840.repl

# Deterministic file capture of UARTE0 (the NRF52840_UART model at
# 0x40002000, easyDMA: true). Second arg = overwrite-existing.
uart0 CreateFileBackend $uartFile true

# Real input path: inject the input fixture into the RAM window @ 0x2002_0000
# BEFORE loading the firmware (and well before RunFor). That window is the
# UPPER 128K of the platform's 256K RAM block, OUTSIDE the firmware's
# memory.x map (RAM = 0x2000_0000 LENGTH 128K), so the stack/.bss never
# collide with the injected bytes. The firmware's NrfUarteShim::alloc_in_region
# reads from this fixed address.
sysbus LoadBinary $input 0x20020000

sysbus LoadELF $bin

# Bounded virtual-time run — the firmware loads its input, computes, and
# EasyDMA-streams its output bytes in microseconds, then spins. No wall-clock
# dependence, fully determinate.
emulation RunFor "0.05"
quit
